From: hmaarrfk <mark.harfouche@conda-forge.org>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: log: provide a gettid() fallback on glibc older than 2.30

1.35.0 added a `[tid:]` field to the NPU_LOG output, implemented with
direct calls to `gettid()` -- in the _LOG macro in
umd/vpu_driver/source/utilities/log.hpp, and in ~500 more places across
the generated umd/level_zero_driver/api/trace/ headers.

glibc only provides the `gettid()` wrapper from 2.30 onwards; the syscall
itself has always existed. Building against an older glibc therefore
fails with

    error: 'gettid' was not declared in this scope; did you mean 'getuid'?

on essentially every translation unit whenever ENABLE_NPU_LOGGING is on,
which is the default. conda-forge builds against a glibc 2.17 sysroot so
that the resulting binaries stay usable on older distributions, and hits
this throughout.

Supply the missing wrapper in log.hpp, guarded on the glibc version.
Every affected call site is covered without touching the generated
headers: they all reach log.hpp through trace_ze_api.hpp. Behaviour on
glibc >= 2.30 is unchanged, since the fallback is not compiled at all
there.
---
 umd/vpu_driver/source/utilities/log.hpp | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)
diff --git a/umd/vpu_driver/source/utilities/log.hpp b/umd/vpu_driver/source/utilities/log.hpp
index c8af5b8..60359c1 100644
--- a/umd/vpu_driver/source/utilities/log.hpp
+++ b/umd/vpu_driver/source/utilities/log.hpp
@@ -12,8 +12,26 @@
 #include <cstdio>
 #include <cstring>
 #include <string_view>
+#include <sys/syscall.h>
 #include <unistd.h>
 
+/*
+ * glibc only provides the gettid() wrapper from 2.30 onwards; the syscall
+ * itself has always been there. Supply the wrapper on older C libraries so
+ * the driver still builds against an older sysroot (conda-forge, for
+ * instance, packages against a glibc 2.17 sysroot to keep the binaries
+ * usable on older distributions).
+ *
+ * Defining it here covers every NPU_LOG call site: the _LOG macro below,
+ * and the generated umd/level_zero_driver/api/trace/ headers, which all
+ * reach this header through trace_ze_api.hpp.
+ */
+#if defined(__GLIBC__) && (__GLIBC__ < 2 || (__GLIBC__ == 2 && __GLIBC_MINOR__ < 30))
+static inline pid_t gettid() {
+    return static_cast<pid_t>(syscall(SYS_gettid));
+}
+#endif
+
 enum LogLevel { QUIET = 0, ERROR, WARNING, INFO };
 
 #define BIT(nr) ((1UL) << (nr))
